10:44:04,880 --> 10:44:10,560
And this is things that are going to occur when your context gets too large, like you have too much information you're passing to the model.

7893
10:44:10,734 --> 10:44:13,188
So the first one is progressive summarization risks.

7894
10:44:13,646 --> 10:44:22,468
So when an AI is asked to condense information over multiple steps, there's going to be information in there that's very important, like dates, percentages, numbers, or even key information.

7895
10:44:23,040 --> 10:44:31,236
the problem is is that as you summarize that information, it doesn't know that that's important information, and it's going to literally make a generic,

7896
10:44:31,920 --> 10:44:41,348
and you're going to lose that information. So the solution is to extract that information out, store it somewhere, and then always inject it back into the next prompt or to the context,

7897
10:44:41,614 --> 10:44:46,052
the exact information so it knows what is the most important information, and we're not losing that out.

7898
10:44:46,958 --> 10:44:48,400
we have loss in the middle effect.

7899
10:44:48,560 --> 10:44:56,872
So if you have if you give a model a lot of data, like let's say 50 pages of data, what it's going to do is it's going to look at the first few pages and the last and it's going to

7900
10:44:56,960 --> 10:44:58,400
miss the middle information.

7901
10:44:58,702 --> 10:45:00,560
And this is just how the model works.

7902
10:45:00,720 --> 10:45:02,212
So it's just what it's going to do.

7903
10:45:02,574 --> 10:45:07,908
So what you can do is break up your data and have it process in sections.

7904
10:45:08,320 --> 10:45:15,040
or if the most important information it uh you know uh is gonna be read only at the start and the beginning, then move that information there.

